From e6b8ce5c21890215d143b1057e9f41d828ee9403 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taekim <taekim@day34.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 02:57:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 48/50] Give the export the column widths the renderer already
 resolves
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`get_column_widths` only reads cells with `col_span == 1`, so a column that
appears exclusively inside a merged cell gets no width and falls back to
1800 HWPUNIT (18pt). On a 서식 table that is most of the grid: the 2025
행정업무운영 편람's 기안문 form table had 6 of its 11 columns at that
placeholder, so a table the renderer draws 393.0pt wide was exported as
342.2pt and a host laying it out from those widths gave 「국무총리」 31pt of
content instead of 71.5 — the label wrapped and the row doubled.

`Layout::resolve_column_widths` already solves this for the renderer, but it
takes `&self` for the dpi and answers in pixels, so a model-only caller
cannot use it. `get_column_widths_resolved` carries the same procedure in
HWPUNIT: skip locally-resized rows, take single-column cells, solve the
merged-cell constraints iteratively, split what stays unknown, give a
constraint's deficit to its last column, default only what remains, then
hand any residual against the table's declared width to the last column.

Measured on that manual: 388 tables, 336 columns at the placeholder become
0, 126 tables change, and the form table's eleven columns match the
renderer's own tree to within 0.2pt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
